    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "S&eacute;zary syndrome",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "S&eacute;zary cells typically show a CD3+/CD4+/CD8&minus; immunophenotype. The loss of CD7 and CD26 is common. Decreased expression of CD2 and/or CD5 is also seen. They are typically &alpha;&beta;&nbsp;T&nbsp;cells. The expression of CD30 is often associated with large cell transformation in mycosis fungoides and S&eacute;zary syndrome. Of note, the enumeration of neoplastic cells by flow cytometry should not be simply based on CD7&minus;/CD4+ or CD26&minus;/CD4+ immunophenotype, because a subset of normal/reactive T&nbsp;cells can be CD7&minus; and/or CD26&minus;. Determination of immunophenotypic aberrancies offers a better way to enumerate neoplastic T&nbsp;cells {32667737}.",
    "source": "Wang Wei&nbsp;-&nbsp;WWang13@mdanderson.org (author on LYM5)",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/64/205/42076.jpg",
